Satoshi (src/lib/theme/fonts/Satoshi-Variable.woff2)

Satoshi, by Indian Type Foundry. Distributed through Fontshare
(https://www.fontshare.com/fonts/satoshi) under the ITF Free Font License,
which is not an open source licence and is not this project's MIT licence.

**The font file is not part of this repository.** `npm run fonts` fetches it
from Fontshare on each machine, and `.gitignore` and `npm run verify:source`
together keep it from being committed.

That is not tidiness. Section 02 of the ITF Free Font License forbids making
the Font Software available through "another font website, font library,
marketplace, repository, download service, application or platform [...]
publicly accessible servers", and a public git repository is exactly that:
anyone cloning it could take the file out and use it on its own. What the
licence does permit, in section 01, is embedding the font in a desktop
application, which is what a built copy of Sill does. So the built application
carries it and the source does not.

If you fork this, `npm install` fetches your own copy direct from Fontshare and
you are bound by that licence yourself, which is the arrangement it describes.

